<BaseLayout title="Coaching — Zeus DeLaCruz" description="One-on-one coaching across the four pillars: operations, performance, evolution, empire.">
<!-- Coaching v2 | /services/coaching/ -->
<section class="hero-full" style="min-height:auto;padding:3rem 0 2rem;">
  <div class="hero-badge">1-ON-1</div>
  <h1 style="font-size:2.8rem;"><span style="color:var(--accent-bright);">4-Pillar</span> Coaching</h1>
  <p class="hero-sub" style="font-size:1.1rem;max-width:600px;">Weekly sessions across all four domains — tech, performance, home, business. You get me, the agents, and the full stack as your personal operating system.</p>
</section>

<section style="padding:2rem 0;">
  <h2 style="color:var(--accent-bright);margin-bottom:1.5rem;">How It Works</h2>
  <div class="card-grid two-col">
    <div class="card"><h4>📋 Pillar Audit</h4><p>First session: we audit all 4 pillars. Where are you strong? Where are you leaking? What's the biggest lever right now?</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>🎯 Quarterly OKRs</h4><p>One objective per pillar per quarter. Not 47 goals. Four. Measurable. The agents track them.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>📅 Weekly Sync</h4><p>60-minute session. Rotates through pillars based on priority. Action items from last week. Blocks removed. Next moves.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>🤖 Agent Access</h4><p>You get NATS access to task SO, HP, LE, GE directly. The agents track your metrics between sessions. Legacy synthesizes cross-domain insights.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>📊 Live Dashboard</h4><p>Your own Grafana dashboard showing pillar metrics — fitness data, cash flow, infrastructure health, business pipeline. Real-time.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h4>🔐 Sovereign Setup</h4><p>Your data lives on your hardware. Not my cloud. Not a SaaS dashboard. Your Grafana, your ClickHouse, your NATS bus.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="padding:2rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);">
  <h2 style="color:var(--accent-bright);margin-bottom:1rem;">Who It's For</h2>
  <p>Builders, operators, founders — people who are already building something and want an operating system for their life, not just another productivity app. You should have at least one active project (tech, business, or homestead) and be willing to instrument it.</p>
  <p style="margin-top:1rem;"><strong>Not for:</strong> people looking for life advice without action. This is hands-on. We build things.</p>
</section>

